"""Write a local model card and artifact integrity receipt after evaluation."""
import hashlib,json,random
from pathlib import Path
root=Path('data/narrative-model/v2')
summary=json.loads((root/'evaluation-summary.json').read_text())
training=json.loads((root/'training-report.json').read_text());cal=json.loads((root/'calibration-report.json').read_text())
rows=[json.loads(l) for l in (root/'train.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()];random.Random(42).shuffle(rows)
style_ids={r['id'] for r in rows[:training['selected_step']*4]}
cal_rows=[json.loads(l) for l in (root/'calibration-train.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()][:cal['selected_step']*4]
exposure={'training_pool':len(rows),'selected_style_examples':training['selected_step']*4,'selected_calibration_examples':len(cal_rows),'unique_sources_in_selected_weights':len(style_ids|{r['id'] for r in cal_rows})}
(root/'exposure.json').write_text(json.dumps(exposure,indent=2))
lines=['# Timekeeper narrative model v2','','Installed locally as `timekeeper-narrative:v2`.', '', '## Selection and training','', 'Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct was selected for feasible float32 CPU training on the i3-10100 / 24 GiB host. Larger installed models are inference-oriented GGUF artifacts. This is a new rank-16 LoRA on the cached base weights, not a rename of the previous adapter.', '',f"The eligible training pool contains {len(rows)} entries, after a finalized-only quality filter and near-duplicate removal. There are 24 validation and 32 final test entries. The selected weights saw {exposure['selected_style_examples']} style examples plus {len(cal_rows)} calibration variants, representing {exposure['unique_sources_in_selected_weights']} distinct source entries. Almost all inputs are reconstructed from completed narratives; this is principally style calibration, not a large corpus of genuine terse-note pairs.",'',f"Style checkpoint: step {training['selected_step']}. Validation loss: {training['base_validation_loss']:.4f} → {training['checkpoints'][-1]['validation_loss']:.4f}. Calibration checkpoint: step {cal['selected_step']}; its validation includes duration-bearing and surname-only variants and therefore uses a different denominator.",'','## Deployed-runtime evaluation','','Identical system prompts and greedy decoding through Ollama. Twelve manually written probes plus 32 held-out corpus examples. No postprocessing of model outputs. The following are automated diagnostics, not a legal/factual accuracy certification.','','| Model | Exact reference* | Preambles | Past-tense starts | Unsupported initials | Durations |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for name,groups in summary.items():
 r=groups['all'];lines.append(f"| {name} | {r['exact_reference_case_insensitive']}/{r['n']} | {r['preambles']} | {r['past_tense_starts']} | {r['initial_failures']} | {r['duration_failures']} |")
lines+=['','*Case-insensitive exact match. Alternative correct wording can fail this metric. Reconstructed inputs make copying relatively easy, so exact-match results must be read alongside the independent probes and full output review.','','## Use','','```bash',"ollama run timekeeper-narrative:v2 'Work done: review lease; email with J. Smith regarding assignment'",'```','','For the exact training prompt, run `python3 scripts/narrative-model/narrate.py "your work notes"` from the project root. The model is available locally; the live app model setting has not been changed.','','All text, weights, comparison outputs and provenance remain local in this directory. Open `comparison.html` for input/reference/output review. Reproduction instructions are in `scripts/narrative-model/README.md`. Drafts still require review, especially sparse or ambiguous notes.']
lines += ['', '## Known development limitation', '', 'At calibration step 20, the shorthand `call w reed re survey` produced `Call with Reed review survey.` The output did not invent an initial, but it misread the relationship between the call and the survey. Duration removal and `rev/analyze` expansion passed the other development probes. See `development-smoke-calibration20.json`; final test results do not erase this observed limitation.']
lines += ['', '## Review of nonmatching final outputs', '', 'Of the five nonmatches: two are acceptable phrasing changes; one leaves `docs` unexpanded; one removes an apparent source typo; and one long entry changes `sequencing of revisions` to `sequencing of reviews`, switches to all caps, and retains supplied WRITE OFF metadata. That long entry needs editing. See `manual-review.json`. Exact matching is not a measure of factual correctness.']
(root/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
receipt={}
for p in list(Path('scripts/narrative-model').glob('*.py'))+[root/'adapter.gguf',root/'calibrated-adapter/adapter_model.safetensors',root/'Modelfile']:
 if p.exists():receipt[str(p)]=hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
(root/'artifact-hashes.json').write_text(json.dumps(receipt,indent=2))
print(root/'REPORT.md')
